      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The fact that minimally invasive surgery for the low back pain is considerably less traumatic has been documented by two broad categories consisted of intradiscal therapeutic and endoscopic procedures. A marked reduction in length of hospitalization has been noted in many cases. Surgeons should select the procedure, or combination of procedures, best suited to benefit of the patient."},
